            <title>[BOOKKEEPER-194] Get correct latency for addEntry operations for JMX.</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/BOOKKEEPER-194</link>
                <project id="12311293" key="BOOKKEEPER">Bookkeeper</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;currently we don&apos;t get the right latency value of add operations. we just compute the latency that entry added to entry log files, but the response sent back to clients only when entries are flushed to journals.&lt;br/&gt;
the right place to compute addEntry latency would be in the WriteCallback.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
